ow according to TVLine  by that point the show was already in  ABC's crosshairs new show runners were  brought in another obvious sign that  castles time was running out the series  hired new show runners Alexi Hawley and  Terrence Paul winner to take the reins  in season 8 hiring new people to run a  show this late in the game is never a  great sign it's even worse that they  made risky changes to the storyline only  to backtrack a few episodes later such  was the case with Castle and Beckett  separation amid outrage from fans Holly  and winter were forced to go on the  defense assuring everyone that nobody  was actually getting divorce  but when Castle and Beckett got back  together by taking their relationship on  the DL even that felt forced unnecessary  and uncreated it seemed like castles new  showrunners we're running with scissors  the show could not survive the negative  press between Khattak sex it rumors of  bad blood on set and the ratings in the  toilet castle limped to the finish line  with a kind of bad press that no show  could shake even if Castle had returned  for a ninth season the show would have  spent the entire time dealing with the  fallout of getting rid of their main  characters it also would have spent a  good chunk of time contending with the  bad press which no doubt would have  ballooned the moment the show took  another dip in ratings in other words by  pulling the plug on Castle now ABC saved  itself from fighting a battle it was  never gonna win sad as it may sound it  was safer to go out on a low note rather  than while scraping the absolute bottom  of the barrel thanks for watching  subscribe to our YouTube channel to  watch more videos like the one you just  saw and leave us a comment to let us  know why you think Castle was really  cancelled
 

